          932
        ],
        "page_id": 18
      }
    ],
    "content": "The imbalance of inadequate national savings compared with the need for increased investment to improve productivity must be corrected.",
    "description": null,
    "id": 5,
    "type": "text"
  },
  {
    "bbox": [
      {
        "coord": [
          736,
          498,
          1403,
          824
        ],
        "page_id": 18
      }
    ],
    "content": "Recent economic statistics have signaled the beginning of a moderate cyclical expansion in the United States. However, economic policies also must consider longer term issues. The imbalance of inadequate national savings compared with the need for increased investment to improve productivity must be corrected. The financial system must be upgraded and strengthened to meet the evolving needs of a dynamic economy. Economic planning must emphasize long-term priorities. Structural adjustments are needed throughout the U.S. economy to prepare to compete in the integrated world economy.",
    "description": null,
    "id": 12,
    "type": "text"
  },
